### Step 0 — Fix output image collision in `rfipconfig-be.yaml`

**File:** `rfipconfig-be.yaml` — **first Build** (`rfipconfig-be-s2i-build`), `spec.output.image` (near the bottom of the first Build, currently:)

```yaml
    image: image-registry.openshift-image-registry.svc:5000/openshift-builds/rfipconfig-be:latest
```

**Change to** (the S2I output is the *builder* image, not the final image — the runtime Build consumes it):

```yaml
    image: image-registry.openshift-image-registry.svc:5000/openshift-builds/rfipconfig-be-builder:latest
```

**Why:** As written, both Builds push to `rfipconfig-be:latest` and the runtime Build references a `rfipconfig-be-builder` tag that nothing produces.

Apply:

```bash
oc apply -f rfipconfig-be.yaml   # re-apply after editing (both Builds edited in Step 3 too — can defer to one apply)
```

---

### Step 1 — Commit runtime files to Git

Work in a clone of `git@hlgithub.hobbylobby.corp:Warehouse/rfipconfig.git`, branch `master`.

**1a. Create directory:**

```bash
cd rfipconfig
mkdir -p runtime
```

**1b. Create `runtime/entrypoint.sh`** — this is the base64 blob from the legacy BuildConfig (`spec.source.dockerfile`, the `RUN echo -n 'IyEvYmluL3No...' | base64 -d` line), decoded:

```sh
#!/bin/sh
dotnet new tool-manifest
dotnet tool install dotnet-certificate-tool
dotnet certificate-tool add --cert /etc/pki/tls/private/auth-clientSecrets.pfx --password $AUTH_PASSWORD
dotnet $APP_DLL --environment $ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT
```

**1c. Create `runtime/Dockerfile`** — multi-stage version of the legacy inline Dockerfile. The `COPY --from=builder` replaces the BuildConfig `source.images[].paths` chained-image copy:

```dockerfile
FROM image-registry.openshift-image-registry.svc:5000/openshift-builds/rfipconfig-be-builder:latest AS builder

FROM quay.hobbylobby.corp/hl-images/hl-dotnet:60-rhel9-latest
USER 0
COPY --from=builder /opt/app-root/app.tar.gz .
RUN tar -xzf app.tar.gz && rm app.tar.gz
RUN yum -y install unixODBC --disablerepo=\* --enablerepo=ubi-9*
RUN curl -fSL -o /tmp/ibm-iaccess.rpm http://hpsatellite01.hobbylobby.corp/pulp/isos/HL/Library/custom/Apache/Tomcat/ibm-iaccess-1.1.0.15-1.0.x86_64.rpm \
 && rpm -i /tmp/ibm-iaccess.rpm && rm /tmp/ibm-iaccess.rpm
COPY entrypoint.sh /tmp/entrypoint.sh
RUN chgrp -R 0 /opt/app-root/* && chmod -R g=u /opt/app-root/* \
 && chgrp 0 /tmp/entrypoint.sh && chmod 754 /tmp/entrypoint.sh
USER 1001
CMD ["/tmp/entrypoint.sh"]
```

> Line 1 mapping: legacy BuildConfig copied `/opt/app-root/` from `rfipconfig-be-builder-#{JENKINS_TAG}#:#{IMAGE_TAG}#`. Here the builder image name is hardcoded (PoC uses fixed `latest` tag). Parameterize with `ARG BUILDER_IMAGE` later once the strategy supports build-args.

**1d. Commit and push:**

```bash
git add runtime/
git commit -m "Runtime image: Dockerfile + extracted entrypoint (BuildConfig migration)"
git push origin master
```

